  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "In an repository with autoversioning turned off, there is not currently a way to tell that a resource has uncommitted changes (mutable head versions). It would be helpful for fedora to expose that a resource is uncommitted via a header or a server generated triple. This feature would be unused in autoversioned repositories.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "We will need to research if ocfl-java has this as a readily retrievable piece of metadata about an object, which would be a prerequisite for this ticket. If it is available, it would need to be communicated up through the stack as a fedora header, but only if autoversioning is off.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
